# Terminology

Use the following terms consistently. The left column is the required form. Do not use the variants
listed on the right unless they appear in code, URLs, or direct quotations from a specification.

| Required term                          | Do not use                                              |
|----------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------|
| Besu                                   | besu, BESU (except in code/URLs/CLI), Hyperledger Besu  |
| dapp                                   | DApp, Dapp, dApp, decentralized application             |
| externally owned account (EOA)         | externally-owned account                                |
| smart contract                         | smartcontract, smart-contract                           |
| proof of stake                         | Proof of Stake, PoS (spell out on first use)            |
| proof of work                          | Proof of Work, PoW (spell out on first use)             |
| proof of authority                     | Proof of Authority, PoA (spell out on first use)        |
| web3                                   | Web3, WEB3 (capitalize only at sentence start)          |
| JSON-RPC                               | json-rpc, Json-RPC, JSONRPC                             |
| onchain / offchain                     | on-chain, off-chain                                     |
| node                                   | full node (unless distinguishing from archive/light)    |
| consensus client                       | consensus layer client, CL client                       |
| execution client                       | execution layer client, EL client                       |
| validator                              | validator node (use "validator" in prose)                |
| early access                           | experimental                                            |

## Consensus protocols (private networks)

| Required term | Do not use                     |
|---------------|--------------------------------|
| IBFT 2.0      | IBFT2, ibft2, iBFT             |
| QBFT          | qbft, Qbft                     |

## Standards and specifications

Besu readers already know what an EIP is. Use the short form `EIP-<number>` in prose.
Do not spell out "Ethereum Improvement Proposal" on first use.
On first mention of a given EIP on a page, link to the specification
(for example, `[EIP-1559](https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-1559)`).
Use the unlinked short form on later mentions of that EIP on the same page.

For other standards (not EIPs), spell out the full name on first use with the
identifier in parentheses. Use the short form on subsequent references.

Examples:

- First use: "[EIP-1559](https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-1559)"
- Subsequent: "EIP-1559"
- First use: "Engine API specification"
- Subsequent: "Engine API"

## Spelling

Pull requests run Vale spelling. A warning means Vale does not recognize a word in a
changed documentation file.

- If the word is a typo, correct it in the documentation.
- If the word is a real term this change introduces, add one pattern to
  `.github/vale/accept.txt` in the same pull request. Vale treats each line as a
  case-sensitive regular expression. Include plurals and possessives in the pattern
  when the page uses them, for example `Openfort(?:'s)?`.
- Leave the shared accept list in `github-actions` unchanged. It already contains the
  terms accepted in the initial audit. New terms stay in this repository's file.
